   "text": "This SMILES was read from the drawing; the stereocentres are partly assigned by assumption rather than read from the wedges. I traced the macrocycle starting at the N-methyl leucine and followed it around the ring.\n\n**Ring path**\n1. N-Me-leucine, with its isobutyl side chain, then C(=O)\u2013N(Me)\u2013CH2\u2013CH=CH\u2013C(=O)\u2013O\u2013CH2\u2013C(CH3)2.\n2. The 1,2-diketone C(=O)C(=O), which links to the piperidine nitrogen of a pipecolic acid unit.\n3. The pipecolic carbonyl, which esterifies the benzylic CH carrying a CH2CH2-(3,4-dimethoxyphenyl) chain.\n4. A meta-disubstituted benzene, whose NH forms a succinyl amide, NH\u2013C(=O)CH2CH2C(=O)\u2013NH.\n5. Phenylglycine, then a phenylalanine whose para-CH2NHC(=O)Ph group carries the benzamide.\n6. Proline, which closes back onto the N-methyl leucine nitrogen.\n\n**Stereochemistry**\n- The wavy C=C bond is drawn with no defined geometry, so I left it unspecified.\n- I assigned L-configuration to leucine, proline and phenylalanine.\n- The pipecolic, phenylglycine and benzylic-carbinol centres are guesses.\n\nSMILES: CC(C)C[C@H]1C(=O)N(C)CC=CC(=O)OCC(C)(C)C(=O)C(=O)N2CCCC[C@H]2C(=O)O[C@H](CCc2ccc(OC)c(OC)c2)c2cccc(c2)NC(=O)CCC(=O)N[C@H](c2ccccc2)C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc2ccc(CNC(=O)c3ccccc3)cc2)C(=O)N2CCC[C@H]2C(=O)N1C"
